Package: linwas-office-look
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: all
Maintainer: mehmedgur <mehmedgrbz11@gmail.com>
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Depends: libreoffice-writer (>= 4:7.3), libreoffice-calc (>= 4:7.3), libreoffice-impress (>= 4:7.3), python3, python3-uno, poppler-utils, fonts-crosextra-carlito, fonts-crosextra-caladea, zenity, pkexec | policykit-1
Recommends: linwas
Conflicts: pardus-ofis-deneyimi, pardus-libreoffice-writer-sade
Replaces: pardus-ofis-deneyimi, pardus-libreoffice-writer-sade
Provides: pardus-ofis-deneyimi
Section: editors
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/mehmedgur/linwas2
Description: Microsoft Office-like look for LibreOffice (Linwas)
 Makes LibreOffice Writer, Calc and Impress feel like Microsoft Office:
 a simple ribbon with few tabs and named groups, an in-window File menu
 (save, save as with format cards, open, recent files, templates, print
 with preview, password protection), Office Open XML as the default
 format, Carlito as the default font and automatic saving.
 .
 Every user can change or turn these off in Linwas (Office › Office look)
 without an administrator password. The simple ribbon is generated from
 the installed LibreOffice at install time and regenerated when
 LibreOffice is upgraded.
